  "body": "# Agent City 0.2.0-rc.3 \u2014 release review draft\n\n**Not yet published or release-qualified.** This next local preview adds selected\nWebOps and VideoOps workflows to the existing real author/reviewer, Kujo execution,\nObserver and replay experience. It is not a universal agent platform certification.\n\n## Changes\n\n- WebOps Reporter \u2192 Copy Chief \u2192 deterministic supplied-evidence report checks.\n- Saved immutable VideoOps Docker image/context and explicit model capability setup.\n- Actual SDK planning, asset resolution and Editor stages, offline isolated render,\n  exact-candidate review, checksum-bound finalization and local download.\n- Bounded acquired-media transport with verified hashes/rights evidence. The initial\n  Mission Command launch surface supports silent original typography/vector work;\n  external speech/music/media generation is not supplied by that form.\n- Corrected planning guidance so inline CSS/SVG/text is composition code rather\n  than a fabricated missing acquired asset. Required real media stays gated.\n- Engine security preflight rejects missing seccomp/AppArmor before model work. Docker Desktop without AppArmor is not a qualified Workcell backend.\n- Updated README and setup/review documentation.\n\n## Requirements and limits\n\nmacOS Intel/Apple Silicon or Linux x64/ARM64; your own Ollama-compatible provider\nor existing authenticated Codex CLI. The installer supplies private Node and pinned\nKujo dependencies. Docker is optional for writing/review and required for isolated\nexecution/rendering. No model accounts, API keys or model weights are bundled.\nVideoOps image measured1.26GB on local amd64; build cache needs extra space.\n\nOriginal artwork is inspired by the supplied references; no protected game assets\nare shipped. Replay does not execute source work. No public hosting, arbitrary\nimported workflow execution, long-duration stability certification or eight-hour\nsoak is claimed. Human review remains required for the exact video candidate.\n\n## Publication checklist\n\n- [ ] Combined real Mission Command production reaches candidate review.\n- [ ] Human reviews that exact candidate, then finalization/download verify its hash.\n- [ ] Final source CI passes build/browser and four-platform installed checks.\n- [ ] Build pinned install/source/manifest/SHA256SUMS assets from that commit.\n- [ ] Publish immutable v0.2.0-rc.3 tag and GitHub prerelease; verify public downloads.\n- [ ] Update the installer link to the newly published version.\n\nThe existing v0.2.0-rc.2 release remains unchanged and available during review.\n"
}
